Package: lunduke-linux-kernel
Version: 7.2.15-lcos33
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 28
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: linux-image-7.2.15-lunduke (= 7.2.15-lcos33)
Recommends: linux-headers-7.2.15-lunduke (= 7.2.15-lcos33)
Description: Lunduke's Linux Kernel for LCOS
 Lunduke's Linux Kernel — LCOS kernel package (ABI lcos33).
 .
 Installs linux-image-7.2.15-lunduke. Headers are recommended for
 building out-of-tree modules.
 .
 lcos33 (LCOS 1.0.1, 2026-11-06) adds, on lcos32: in-kernel
 WireGuard; IPv6 policy routing (MULTIPLE_TABLES + SUBTREES);
 OpenVPN Data Channel Offload; IPv4 IPsec ESP/AH (IPv6 IPsec is
 already on); FQ and CAKE qdiscs; the Ralink/rt2x00 family
 including RT73USB (LCOS#194) plus RT2800/RT2500/RT2400 USB and
 PCI; ATH5K; Atheros L1C/L1E; the VMware balloon; Corsair, Razer,
 Glorious, and Plantronics HID; VLAN, macvlan, and ipvlan;
 Samsung Galaxy Book, MSI WMI platform, and TUXEDO/Uniwill laptop
 support. Carry these options into the 7.3 and 7.4 configs for
 LCOS 1.1 (those configs are not in this repo yet). Same
 7.2.15-lunduke kernel release.
 .
 lcos32 (LCOS 1.0.1, editor 2026-11-04) adds, on lcos31, the ACPI
 Smart Battery System driver (ACPI_SBS=m: sbs, sbshc) for the 2014
 MacBook Air battery (LCOS#191). Same 7.2.15-lunduke kernel release.
 .
 lcos31 (LCOS 1.0.1, editor 2026-11-03) adds, on lcos30, driver
 modules: Synaptics RMI4 HID touchpads (HID_RMI, RMI4_I2C, LCOS#182),
 Intel 10GbE X520 (IXGBE, IXGBEVF, LCOS#183), traffic control for the
 libvirt default network (HTB, TBF, ingress, fq_codel, SFQ, u32,
 flower, fw, csum/gact/mirred/police actions, LCOS#184), and Broadcom
 b44 wired plus Intel 3945/4965 Wi-Fi (B44, IWLEGACY, IWL3945,
 IWL4965, LCOS#187). Same 7.2.15-lunduke kernel release.
 .
 lcos30 (LCOS 1.0.1, editor 2026-11-02) moves to upstream Linux 7.2.15,
 the final 7.2.y stable release (9 stable releases of fixes over 7.2.6,
 including the Dell XPS 13 DX13260 speaker-ID fix from 7.2.10). The
 kernel release is now 7.2.15-lunduke, so the package names change to
 linux-image-7.2.15-lunduke and linux-headers-7.2.15-lunduke. They
 install beside 7.2.6-lunduke, which stays installed as a GRUB fallback.
 Config is lcos28 plus, from the lcos29 config (PR #25), the Ensoniq
 ES1371 sound driver for VMware guests (CONFIG_SND_ENS1371=m), plus
 Intel Touch Host Controller touchscreens (INTEL_THC_HID, INTEL_QUICKI2C,
 INTEL_QUICKSPI =m), haptic touchpads (HID_HAPTIC=y) and compressed RAM
 swap (ZRAM=m with zstd). No source patches. lcos29 (7.2.6) was never
 built.
 .
 lcos28 adds, on lcos27: the Apple SPI keyboard and trackpad driver
 (CONFIG_KEYBOARD_APPLESPI=m, applespi, ACPI APP000D) for the 12-inch
 MacBook (MacBook8,1, 2015) and later SPI MacBook/MacBook Pro models.
 It keeps the same 7.2.6-lunduke kernel release.
 .
 lcos27 adds, on lcos25: ExpressCard/eSATA support (SATA_SIL24=m,
 SATA_MV=m, HOTPLUG_PCI_ACPI=y, USB_XHCI_PCI_RENESAS=m). It keeps the
 same 7.2.6-lunduke kernel release. lcos26 was a per-build naming
 experiment that was backed out and is not a base for lcos27.
 .
 lcos25 adds, on lcos24: UDF filesystem (CONFIG_UDF_FS=m, DVD/Blu-ray
 and packet-written media, LCOS#149), LED flash class
 (CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS_FLASH=m) and the LED brightness_hw_changed sysfs
 attribute (CONFIG_LEDS_BRIGHTNESS_HW_CHANGED=y, a bool) needed by the
 out-of-tree tuxedo-drivers keyboard backlight (kernel#14).
 .
 lcos24 adds, on lcos23 (Ubuntu 26.10 hardware gap, editor 2026-10-15):
 Intel IPU3/IPU6 laptop cameras with VSC and common sensors, Logitech
 HID++/Unifying, joydev/xpad/Steam Controller HID, Intel PMC/PCH
 thermal helpers, AMD HSMP and TAC5XX2 SoundWire codec, ACPI ambient
 light sensor. INPUT_AMD_SFH_TABLETMODE is 7.3-only and was skipped.
 .
 lcos23 adds, on lcos22 (LCOS#141): Chromebook touchpad support for
 the Acer C720 and other 2013-era Chromebooks, chromeos_laptop (creates
 the I2C touchpad device on stock/legacy firmware) and cyapa (Cypress
 APA touchpads), both =m.
 .
 lcos22 adds, on lcos21 (LCOS#138): Realtek USB Wi-Fi 6/6E/7 rtw89
 RTL8852CU (TP-Link), RTL8852BU, RTL8851BU, RTL8922AU, and PCIe
 RTL8814AE (rtw88), all =m.
 .
 lcos21 adds, on lcos20: Intel VMD (CONFIG_VMD=m) for NVMe behind
 Intel Volume Management Device (Dell "RAID On"), and PCIe native
 hotplug (CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE=y).
 .
 lcos20 adds, on lcos19: exFAT filesystem (CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=m, default
 iocharset utf8, LCOS#131) for USB sticks, SD cards and Ventoy drives.
 .
 lcos19 adds, on lcos18 (LCOS#115/#118 AMD audit vs Ubuntu generic):
 radeon (pre-GCN Radeons, CIK fallback), vga_switcheroo, DC for SI,
 amdgpu userptr and HSA/KFD, compressed firmware loading, AMD platform
 GPIO/I2C (piix4), devfreq. See docs/amdgpu-audit-lcos19.md.
 .
 lcos18 adds, on frozen lcos17: dm-crypt with AES-NI/XTS/ESSIV and
 the AF_ALG skcipher/hash interfaces for LUKS disk encryption
 (LCOS#123), UHID for Bluetooth LE mice and keyboards (LCOS#120), and
 Synaptics RMI4 F11/F3A touchpad functions (LCOS#121).
 .
 lcos17 added the SMB2/SMB3 network file system client on
 lcos16: cifs (CONFIG_CIFS=m, CONFIG_CIFS_XATTR=y, LCOS#111), so
 Windows, Samba, and NAS shares mount with cifs-utils. SMB1 legacy
 dialects (CIFS_ALLOW_INSECURE_LEGACY), SMB Direct, and the ksmbd
 server stay off. Rust left off (No Forced Rust). No firmware blob is
 included. Proprietary NVIDIA is not included.
 .
 LCOS 0.8 ISOs shipped 7.2.6-lcos12; that config stays frozen.
 lcos13 through lcos17 stay frozen. This package is the
 lcos28 revision of the same linux-image-7.2.6-lunduke name. On earlier
 LCOS releases that still ship a Distro kernel, installing this
 metapackage adds a GRUB entry alongside it.
